% Sync: The Drawbridge (one crosses and lowers the bridge; mist, then throw)
%
% A sentinel - a heavy machine - stands on a ledge beyond a gulf. Nothing
% moves it. The drawbridge over the gulf is raised, and its winch is a
% plate on the far pier. Three companions: the player and the mage pick one
% skill each from seven; the porter only knows Turn to Mist. Nothing can be
% done from the dock - the ledge is out of sight - so one companion crosses
% alone and lowers the bridge, and the others walk over and finish it.
%
%   dock ==gulf (a gap) + drawbridge (a door)== pier [winch] --- ledge (sentinel, cliff)
%                                                 |                 :
%                                              overlook ...gap...
%
% The moment: the porter turns the sentinel to mist - for a moment it is
% not heavy. The moment lasts through the next cast by anyone, so the very
% next cast must be the one that throws it: mist, then throw, back to back.
%
% Obstacles and every method:
%   the gulf       nobody walks over it while the bridge is up. Blink onto
%                  the pier, or lightning-flash there (a dash). On the pier,
%                  step on the winch: the drawbridge comes down for good.
%   the sentinel   right after the porter's mist, knock it off the ledge:
%                  into the cliff with a fireball or a shield bash (from the
%                  pier), a tidal wave (on the ledge), a vortex on the
%                  cliff; or hook it from the overlook, across the gap: it
%                  falls in. Or short it, no mist at all: a tidal wave soaks
%                  it, a lightning flash jolts it.
%
% Traps:
%   - no line of sight from the dock: nothing is done from the near side;
%   - the crossing skills move only their caster and throw nothing;
%   - heavy, the sentinel does not budge: a push without the mist right
%     before it does nothing, and so does a push after any other cast; a
%     hook on it drags the hooker to it;
%   - a dry jolt only stuns a machine: the flasher who crossed has mana
%     for one more flash, and it only shorts the sentinel once it is wet;
%   - a vortex on the cliff takes everyone on the ledge, friends included.
%
% Hypothesis (design.md): no single skill wins; 20 of 49 assignments win
% (each crossing skill with each thrower, either seat), by 11 methods.

% === Areas ===
region(dock).
region(pier).
region(ledge).
region(overlook).
gap(dock, pier).
doorway(dock, pier, drawbridge).
connected(pier, ledge).
connected(pier, overlook).
gap(overlook, ledge).

lineOfSight(dock, pier).
lineOfSight(pier, ledge).
lineOfSight(overlook, ledge).

% The route, for leaps (passage): only forward.
progress(dock, 0).
progress(pier, 1).
progress(ledge, 2).
progress(overlook, 2).

% === Features ===
feature(pier, winch, lower).
plate(winch).
effect(lower, target, open(drawbridge)).
door(drawbridge).
feature(ledge, cliff, chasm).

% === Companions ===
role(player, player).
role(mage, companion).
role(porter, companion).
at(player, dock).
at(mage, dock).
at(porter, dock).
mana(player, 4).
mana(mage, 4).
knows(porter, turnToMist).

% === The sentinel ===
role(sentinel, enemy).
at(sentinel, ledge).
tag(sentinel, machine).
tag(sentinel, heavy).

% === Default kit: one skill each (combos replans the whole matrix) ===
knows(player, blink).
knows(mage, fireball).

% === Victory ===
% Someone crosses and lowers the bridge, then the sentinel goes.
win :- if(), do(lowerBridge, drop).

lowerBridge :-
    if(canAct(?a), not(at(?a, pier))), do(reach(?a, pier), stepOn(?a, winch), opened(drawbridge)).
opened(?d) :- if(open(?d)), do().

% Mist, then throw: the porter's moment, and the very next cast knocks it
% off the ledge (or drags it across the gap).
drop :-
    if(),
    do(cast(porter, turnToMist, sentinel), sendDown(sentinel, porter), confirmStopped(sentinel)).
% Or short it: soaked, then jolted.
drop :- if(), do(conduct(sentinel)).

funExpect(single_actor_plans, atMost, 0).

% === Choice: one skill each, from seven (htn_components combos) ===
% The porter keeps turnToMist.
comboSeat(player, 1).
comboSeat(mage, 1).
comboPool(blink).
comboPool(lightningFlash).
comboPool(fireball).
comboPool(tidalWave).
comboPool(hook).
comboPool(vortex).
comboPool(shieldBash).
comboMinWins(8).
comboMinMethods(4).

goals(win).
